1
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:52,840
Changxuan.

2
00:01:53,200 --> 00:01:54,159
Tell me everything

3
00:01:54,799 --> 00:01:56,620
that's happened between you and Pingjun.

4
00:01:58,620 --> 00:01:59,959
Pingjun remembers...

5
00:02:00,159 --> 00:02:01,540
This mentions her mother's death.

6
00:02:01,540 --> 00:02:02,540
What's the full story?

7
00:02:03,019 --> 00:02:03,420
You said

8
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:04,900
her mother died in an accident!

9
00:02:05,019 --> 00:02:05,819
Exactly.

10
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:07,540
Pingjun's pregnant.

11
00:02:07,739 --> 00:02:09,180
How could she manage on her own?

12
00:02:09,539 --> 00:02:10,199
You...

13
00:02:10,719 --> 00:02:11,300
Changxuan!

14
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:11,780
Changxuan!

15
00:02:11,780 --> 00:02:12,360
Changxuan!

16
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:13,060
Changxuan!

17
00:02:16,340 --> 00:02:17,240
Excuse me.

18
00:02:17,300 --> 00:02:18,539
Where's the station exit?

19
00:02:18,819 --> 00:02:19,319
Over there.

20
00:02:19,860 --> 00:02:20,199
Thanks.

21
00:02:20,340 --> 00:02:20,580
Sure.

22
00:02:20,620 --> 00:02:21,400
Excuse me.

23
00:02:22,039 --> 00:02:22,479
One ticket

24
00:02:22,479 --> 00:02:24,080
on the next train to Tianjin, please.

25
00:02:24,259 --> 00:02:25,520
The last one's gone.

26
00:02:25,580 --> 00:02:26,280
No more trains.

27
00:02:26,680 --> 00:02:27,620
Martial law starts tomorrow.

28
00:02:27,680 --> 00:02:28,580
All services suspended.

29
00:02:28,900 --> 00:02:29,719
Until when?

30
00:02:30,219 --> 00:02:31,020
Hard to say.

31
00:02:33,879 --> 00:02:34,479
Thank you.

32
00:02:51,460 --> 00:02:52,020
Hey, sweetheart.

33
00:02:52,379 --> 00:02:53,199
All alone?

34
00:02:53,800 --> 00:02:54,800
Where are you headed?

35
00:02:55,319 --> 00:02:56,180
No trains, eh?

36
00:02:56,479 --> 00:02:57,180
I've got a car.

37
00:02:57,439 --> 00:02:58,039
Come with me.

38
00:02:58,659 --> 00:03:00,159
I'll take you anywhere you like.

39
00:03:01,259 --> 00:03:01,800
Sweetheart.

40
00:03:02,020 --> 00:03:02,919
Don't run off.

41
00:03:03,080 --> 00:03:05,199
Stay and keep us company.

42
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:07,479
Let go!

43
00:03:10,800 --> 00:03:11,719
I'm warning you.

44
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,900
There are patrols all around here.

45
00:03:14,060 --> 00:03:15,240
I'll call for help!

46
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:17,439
Patrols?

47
00:03:17,699 --> 00:03:18,500
Sweetheart,

48
00:03:18,560 --> 00:03:20,360
I'll be your personal policeman.

49
00:03:20,719 --> 00:03:22,360
Come tell me all about it in my arms.

50
00:03:22,360 --> 00:03:23,000
Let go!

51
00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:24,580
Let go!

52
00:03:44,560 --> 00:03:46,099
Wenbo, look!

53
00:03:46,699 --> 00:03:47,699
What are you doing?

54
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:49,060
Stop!

55
00:03:53,020 --> 00:03:53,860
Pingjun?

56
00:03:58,759 --> 00:03:59,400
Pingjun!

57
00:03:59,960 --> 00:04:00,520
Pingjun?

58
00:04:00,819 --> 00:04:01,780
What's she doing here?

59
00:04:01,860 --> 00:04:02,860
Get her to a hospital!

60
00:04:03,259 --> 00:04:03,659
Right!

61
00:04:13,120 --> 00:04:13,659
Sir.

62
00:04:14,139 --> 00:04:14,699
Any news?

63
00:04:15,599 --> 00:04:16,480
A rickshaw puller said

64
00:04:16,699 --> 00:04:17,699
he took a woman

65
00:04:17,699 --> 00:04:18,319
whose build and looks

66
00:04:18,319 --> 00:04:19,560
closely matched Ma'am's.

67
00:04:19,819 --> 00:04:20,579
He dropped her off

68
00:04:20,579 --> 00:04:21,980
at the south gate.

69
00:04:22,220 --> 00:04:23,319
We sent a team

70
00:04:23,560 --> 00:04:24,660
to search that way,

71
00:04:24,819 --> 00:04:25,899
but found no leads.

72
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:28,439
Nothing at all?

73
00:04:29,500 --> 00:04:30,279
Stations and wharves

74
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:31,800
all have checkpoints now.

75
00:04:32,259 --> 00:04:33,180
Any news comes in,

76
00:04:33,439 --> 00:04:34,439
and we'll report at once.

77
00:04:38,879 --> 00:04:40,040
Widen the search.

78
00:04:40,100 --> 00:04:41,439
Follow every lead.

79
00:04:42,040 --> 00:04:42,860
If you hear anything,

80
00:04:42,860 --> 00:04:43,819
tell me right away.

81
00:04:44,139 --> 00:04:44,800
Remember,

82
00:04:45,139 --> 00:04:46,360
her safety comes first.

83
00:04:47,300 --> 00:04:48,500
If she won't come back,

84
00:04:48,980 --> 00:04:49,720
don't force her.

85
00:04:50,439 --> 00:04:51,300
You have my word.

86
00:04:51,540 --> 00:04:52,420
I'll go now.

87
00:04:58,319 --> 00:04:59,540
Try not to worry.

88
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:01,040
Look after yourself.

89
00:05:03,279 --> 00:05:03,839
Let's go.

90
00:05:43,699 --> 00:05:44,600
Pingjun?

91
00:05:45,939 --> 00:05:46,839
You're awake.

92
00:05:48,939 --> 00:05:50,019
Hanzhi?

93
00:05:53,339 --> 00:05:54,959
What are you doing here?

94
00:05:56,199 --> 00:05:57,600
I'm in nearby Siping,

95
00:05:58,019 --> 00:05:59,339
setting up a charity.

96
00:06:00,139 --> 00:06:01,079
By chance,

97
00:06:01,560 --> 00:06:03,060
I found you in the street last night

98
00:06:03,899 --> 00:06:05,300
and brought you to the hospital.

99
00:06:07,339 --> 00:06:08,199
The hospital?

100
00:06:15,399 --> 00:06:16,040
Let go!

101
00:06:21,779 --> 00:06:22,680
The baby...

102
00:06:27,459 --> 00:06:28,879
My baby...

103
00:06:32,139 --> 00:06:32,899
The baby...

104
00:06:34,579 --> 00:06:35,879
Is my baby all right?

105
00:06:44,699 --> 00:06:45,500
Pingjun.

106
00:06:46,100 --> 00:06:47,300
Listen to me.

107
00:06:49,079 --> 00:06:50,620
You lost a lot of blood.

108
00:06:51,259 --> 00:06:52,639
The doctor did all he could.

109
00:06:53,699 --> 00:06:54,519
The baby...

110
00:06:56,180 --> 00:06:57,379
The baby is gone...

111
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:12,399
That can't be.

112
00:07:15,300 --> 00:07:16,579
My baby's still here.

113
00:07:19,259 --> 00:07:21,279
I know it's still here.

114
00:07:22,699 --> 00:07:25,360
My baby's still here.

115
00:07:26,639 --> 00:07:27,500
He's still here.

116
00:07:27,720 --> 00:07:28,620
Please, don't.

117
00:07:31,399 --> 00:07:32,259
What are you doing?

118
00:07:32,399 --> 00:07:33,439
I'll see the doctor.

119
00:07:33,500 --> 00:07:34,019
Please, don't.

120
00:07:34,339 --> 00:07:34,939
I need the doctor.

121
00:07:35,060 --> 00:07:35,620
Pingjun!

122
00:07:35,620 --> 00:07:36,279
Let go!

123
00:07:36,279 --> 00:07:37,439
I need to see the doctor!

124
00:07:37,519 --> 00:07:38,399
Calm down.

125
00:07:38,480 --> 00:07:39,339
Please, calm down.

126
00:07:39,420 --> 00:07:40,240
Please, don't...

127
00:08:21,019 --> 00:08:21,660
Changxuan.

128
00:08:22,259 --> 00:08:23,199
About that fire,

129
00:08:23,199 --> 00:08:24,060
I've found out more.

130
00:08:26,939 --> 00:08:27,740
Among the things recovered

131
00:08:27,740 --> 00:08:29,060
was a charred button.

132
00:08:29,160 --> 00:08:29,920
Could it be linked

133
00:08:29,920 --> 00:08:30,339
to the one

134
00:08:30,339 --> 00:08:31,139
Pingjun left behind?

135
00:08:40,960 --> 00:08:41,460
But this one

136
00:08:41,460 --> 00:08:42,440
was likely lost by one of

137
00:08:42,440 --> 00:08:43,320
our men fighting the fire.

138
00:08:50,399 --> 00:08:51,580
There's another possibility.

139
00:08:57,019 --> 00:08:57,700
Captain.

140
00:08:58,360 --> 00:08:59,820
The Yus are making quite a stir.

141
00:09:00,299 --> 00:09:01,580
Yu Changxuan's men.

142
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:02,779
They've searched

143
00:09:02,779 --> 00:09:04,179
almost every inch of Nanhuai.

144
00:09:04,379 --> 00:09:05,580
Bus stations, train stations,

145
00:09:05,580 --> 00:09:07,960
every wharf has men checking travelers.

146
00:09:08,399 --> 00:09:09,200
They're after someone.

147
00:09:11,259 --> 00:09:12,080
Someone?

148
00:09:12,580 --> 00:09:13,379
Yes, sir.

149
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:14,659
They're looking for

150
00:09:15,559 --> 00:09:17,139
Yu Changxuan's wife.

151
00:09:17,580 --> 00:09:18,460
Apparently,

152
00:09:18,460 --> 00:09:19,759
she ran away from home out of the blue.

153
00:09:31,179 --> 00:09:32,200
She remembers.

154
00:09:34,379 --> 00:09:35,679
She must have remembered.

155
00:09:36,899 --> 00:09:37,559
I'm not following.

156
00:09:38,120 --> 00:09:39,879
Remembered... what?

157
00:09:41,580 --> 00:09:42,620
Send men to find her.

158
00:09:43,259 --> 00:09:44,159
We must beat Yu Changxuan

159
00:09:44,159 --> 00:09:44,840
to her.

160
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:46,600
Yes, sir.

161
00:09:47,379 --> 00:09:48,759
I'll see to it at once.

162
00:09:56,799 --> 00:09:57,879
Yu Changxuan.

163
00:09:59,559 --> 00:10:00,960
I always knew

164
00:10:03,379 --> 00:10:04,539
that whatever you gained

165
00:10:04,539 --> 00:10:05,659
through your lies

166
00:10:06,840 --> 00:10:08,559
would be lost to you one day.

167
00:10:11,059 --> 00:10:12,980
Once Pingjun knows the truth,

168
00:10:14,480 --> 00:10:16,120
how could she bear

169
00:10:16,120 --> 00:10:16,679
to share

170
00:10:16,679 --> 00:10:18,620
a home with you?

171
00:11:39,679 --> 00:11:40,419
Pingjun.

172
00:11:44,919 --> 00:11:46,399
Where are you?

173
00:11:57,620 --> 00:12:00,080
As spring turned to summer in 1927,

174
00:12:00,120 --> 00:12:01,820
the revolutionary army advanced,

175
00:12:01,899 --> 00:12:03,059
nearing Beijing and Tianjin.

176
00:12:03,139 --> 00:12:04,919
The central government's defeats

177
00:12:05,059 --> 00:12:06,600
spread panic within its ranks.

178
00:12:06,840 --> 00:12:07,840
General Xu

179
00:12:07,840 --> 00:12:09,480
formed a northern military government,

180
00:12:09,700 --> 00:12:11,539
hoping to unite the northern warlords

181
00:12:11,539 --> 00:12:12,940
for a final stand.

182
00:12:13,179 --> 00:12:13,960
Meanwhile,

183
00:12:14,159 --> 00:12:15,399
he let the Japanese envoy

184
00:12:15,399 --> 00:12:17,639
make peace overtures to the south

185
00:12:17,879 --> 00:12:19,460
to buy himself time.

186
00:12:19,740 --> 00:12:20,940
Years of warfare

187
00:12:21,059 --> 00:12:22,220
sent prices soaring

188
00:12:22,360 --> 00:12:23,500
and left people destitute.

189
00:12:23,659 --> 00:12:25,840
Countless civilians lost their homes.

190
00:12:26,159 --> 00:12:28,440
Patriots took to the streets,

191
00:12:28,580 --> 00:12:30,179
crying, "Down with the warlords!

192
00:12:30,240 --> 00:12:31,960
End the civil war!"

193
00:12:32,120 --> 00:12:34,440
Their protests were brutally crushed.

194
00:12:34,659 --> 00:12:36,100
As we've just heard,

195
00:12:36,759 --> 00:12:38,840
the situation is grave.

196
00:12:40,240 --> 00:12:41,759
The central government

197
00:12:41,799 --> 00:12:43,100
is pressing us again

198
00:12:43,100 --> 00:12:44,860
to declare which side we're on.

199
00:12:46,360 --> 00:12:48,539
I'd like to hear your views first.

200
00:12:52,460 --> 00:12:53,519
If you ask me,

201
00:12:54,200 --> 00:12:55,559
we take no side.

202
00:12:55,759 --> 00:12:58,120
We hold our ground here in Nanhuai.

203
00:12:58,679 --> 00:13:00,899
Our land and people must come first.

204
00:13:02,559 --> 00:13:04,220
Xiaoxian has a point.

205
00:13:04,539 --> 00:13:06,000
But it's a delicate situation.

206
00:13:06,700 --> 00:13:08,539
If we refuse the central government,

207
00:13:08,799 --> 00:13:11,620
we risk making ourselves a target.

208
00:13:14,259 --> 00:13:14,899
Changxuan?

209
00:13:17,360 --> 00:13:18,720
With foreign powers closing in,

210
00:13:19,360 --> 00:13:20,820
if we blindly obey the government

211
00:13:21,080 --> 00:13:23,080
and turn our guns on our own people,

212
00:13:23,419 --> 00:13:24,879
we risk making enemies of the south

213
00:13:24,879 --> 00:13:26,419
and losing the people's support.

214
00:13:27,820 --> 00:13:28,940
I agree with Changxuan.

215
00:13:30,340 --> 00:13:31,179
But Chu Wenfu's

216
00:13:31,179 --> 00:13:32,659
conference in Changling

217
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:33,899
cannot be taken lightly.

218
00:13:34,519 --> 00:13:35,840
Someone must negotiate

219
00:13:36,179 --> 00:13:36,860
to give our army

220
00:13:37,139 --> 00:13:38,600
more time to prepare.

221
00:13:41,500 --> 00:13:43,000
Good. It's settled, then.

222
00:13:44,419 --> 00:13:44,899
All right.

223
00:13:44,980 --> 00:13:45,899
Send it over when it's time.

224
00:13:50,720 --> 00:13:51,279
Changxuan.

225
00:13:53,039 --> 00:13:54,519
Our men at the Siping front

226
00:13:54,919 --> 00:13:56,399
spotted a woman in town

227
00:13:56,879 --> 00:13:57,639
who looked

228
00:13:59,039 --> 00:13:59,879
a bit like Pingjun.

229
00:14:00,600 --> 00:14:01,879
They lost her in the crowd.

230
00:14:02,220 --> 00:14:03,240
We can't be sure yet.

231
00:14:03,940 --> 00:14:04,779
Siping?

232
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:08,639
Get the car.

233
00:14:10,159 --> 00:14:10,639
Changxuan.

234
00:14:11,840 --> 00:14:13,179
The army's facing a crisis.

235
00:14:13,600 --> 00:14:14,919
Everyone's watching you.

236
00:14:14,940 --> 00:14:16,200
Leaving Nanhuai now

237
00:14:16,779 --> 00:14:17,519
would be unwise.

238
00:14:18,559 --> 00:14:19,200
Besides,

239
00:14:19,940 --> 00:14:21,220
it was a misunderstanding

240
00:14:21,220 --> 00:14:21,980
that made her leave.

241
00:14:22,679 --> 00:14:23,879
If you turn up unannounced,

242
00:14:24,480 --> 00:14:25,639
she might flee even farther.

243
00:14:29,399 --> 00:14:30,240
Don't worry.

244
00:14:31,360 --> 00:14:32,940
I promise I'll bring her back.

245
00:14:35,019 --> 00:14:36,340
I'm counting on you, Ruitong.

246
00:15:00,179 --> 00:15:01,279
Let's pick out some flowers, shall we?

247
00:15:01,279 --> 00:15:01,960
Hello.

248
00:15:05,139 --> 00:15:06,980
We'd like to look at your flowers.

249
00:15:07,960 --> 00:15:08,679
Of course.

250
00:15:09,820 --> 00:15:11,120
Come on, sweetie.

251
00:15:18,220 --> 00:15:19,440
Isn't this pretty?

252
00:15:29,639 --> 00:15:30,220
Look.

253
00:15:32,620 --> 00:15:33,960
How much is this?

254
00:15:35,299 --> 00:15:37,980
It's a gift. Take it.

255
00:15:39,019 --> 00:15:40,320
Oh, you're so kind.

256
00:15:40,620 --> 00:15:41,559
Thank you.

257
00:15:42,580 --> 00:15:44,440
Isn't she lovely, little one?

258
00:15:54,679 --> 00:15:55,539
I'll take over.

259
00:15:55,840 --> 00:15:57,259
Go and get that cut bandaged.

260
00:15:58,840 --> 00:16:00,799
It's just a cut. It'll heal soon.

261
00:16:02,320 --> 00:16:03,720
Your baby is watching over you.

262
00:16:04,100 --> 00:16:05,299
The little guardian angel

263
00:16:05,480 --> 00:16:07,100
would want you to be well.

264
00:16:07,519 --> 00:16:08,700
Your being happy

265
00:16:08,879 --> 00:16:10,720
would console this little soul.

266
00:16:15,340 --> 00:16:16,299
I see.

267
00:16:17,299 --> 00:16:17,840
Captain.

268
00:16:18,440 --> 00:16:19,299
One more thing.

269
00:16:19,740 --> 00:16:20,899
With this conference

270
00:16:21,279 --> 00:16:22,860
bringing so many people here,

271
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:24,919
and Interior controlling the news,

272
00:16:25,500 --> 00:16:26,600
we followed custom

273
00:16:26,919 --> 00:16:28,519
and charged several news outlets

274
00:16:28,700 --> 00:16:30,919
a fee to ease them past the censors.

275
00:16:31,460 --> 00:16:32,460
Please take a look.

276
00:16:50,039 --> 00:16:51,659
Who imparted all these filthy, little

277
00:16:52,519 --> 00:16:53,299
schemes to you?

278
00:16:53,379 --> 00:16:54,299
Please, sir.

279
00:16:54,799 --> 00:16:57,220
I... It's the usual arrangement.

280
00:16:57,960 --> 00:16:58,700
I thought...

281
00:16:58,919 --> 00:16:59,759
Thought you'd win my favor?

282
00:17:02,200 --> 00:17:04,119
You think this paltry sum

283
00:17:05,559 --> 00:17:07,059
is enough to cozy up to me?

284
00:17:13,740 --> 00:17:15,319
Spare me, sir! Please!

285
00:17:15,500 --> 00:17:16,339
Useless fool!

286
00:17:17,079 --> 00:17:17,539
Get out!

287
00:17:29,579 --> 00:17:31,359
What a temper.

288
00:17:33,259 --> 00:17:34,319
If you ask me, Captain Jiang,

289
00:17:34,380 --> 00:17:36,740
it's not corruption you find unbearable.

290
00:17:36,859 --> 00:17:39,480
It's the fact that there's still no word of Ye Pingjun

291
00:17:39,700 --> 00:17:41,359
that is driving you mad.

292
00:17:42,259 --> 00:17:43,740
You're just taking it out on them.

293
00:17:44,380 --> 00:17:45,220
My affairs

294
00:17:46,740 --> 00:17:47,900
are no concern of yours.

295
00:17:54,440 --> 00:17:55,240
Tell me.

296
00:17:55,660 --> 00:17:57,339
All this elaborate plotting

297
00:17:57,339 --> 00:17:58,819
against Yu Changxuan...

298
00:17:59,859 --> 00:18:01,380
Is it really

299
00:18:01,660 --> 00:18:03,740
to get revenge on him and his family,

300
00:18:04,339 --> 00:18:05,700
or is it

301
00:18:07,880 --> 00:18:09,680
to win Ye Pingjun back?

302
00:18:12,500 --> 00:18:13,319
Miss Tao.

303
00:18:14,400 --> 00:18:15,339
You seem to have forgotten.

304
00:18:16,319 --> 00:18:17,140
Everything

305
00:18:17,680 --> 00:18:18,640
between you and me

306
00:18:18,640 --> 00:18:19,759
is reciprocity.

307
00:18:21,640 --> 00:18:22,720
We've never been

308
00:18:22,720 --> 00:18:24,740
a devoted, loving couple.

309
00:18:28,359 --> 00:18:29,579
You have no right

310
00:18:30,720 --> 00:18:32,059
to meddle with my feelings.

311
00:18:36,519 --> 00:18:37,420
Jiang Xueting.

312
00:18:38,380 --> 00:18:40,279
Your swift rise through government

313
00:18:40,619 --> 00:18:42,619
and your secure position today

314
00:18:43,039 --> 00:18:44,400
owe a great deal

315
00:18:44,619 --> 00:18:46,460
to the money my family spent

316
00:18:46,779 --> 00:18:48,059
greasing palms for you.

317
00:18:48,380 --> 00:18:49,480
I'm warning you.

318
00:18:50,319 --> 00:18:51,140
Don't let

319
00:18:51,140 --> 00:18:52,559
your personal feelings

320
00:18:53,019 --> 00:18:55,099
ruin everything we've planned.

321
00:18:56,900 --> 00:18:58,019
I gave my word,

322
00:18:59,619 --> 00:19:00,519
and I'll keep it.

323
00:19:02,319 --> 00:19:03,440
My private life, however,

324
00:19:04,759 --> 00:19:05,740
is outside your remit.

325
00:19:08,339 --> 00:19:09,500
You'd better keep your word.

326
00:19:20,079 --> 00:19:20,859
No sign of her, sir.

327
00:19:20,859 --> 00:19:21,720
Split up. Search the alleys

328
00:19:21,720 --> 00:19:22,140
up ahead.

329
00:19:22,140 --> 00:19:22,779
Yes, sir.

330
00:19:59,140 --> 00:19:59,859
Excuse me.

331
00:20:01,220 --> 00:20:02,380
Where did you get these hostas?

332
00:20:02,619 --> 00:20:03,700
S-Sir...

333
00:20:03,700 --> 00:20:05,460
I... I bought these flowers.

334
00:20:06,140 --> 00:20:06,819
Where?

335
00:20:07,099 --> 00:20:08,240
Two streets ahead,

336
00:20:08,380 --> 00:20:09,880
there's a new flower shop.

337
00:20:10,099 --> 00:20:12,039
The owner loves hostas.

338
00:20:12,140 --> 00:20:13,299
She has a heart of gold.

339
00:20:13,420 --> 00:20:14,539
She often holds charity sales

340
00:20:14,720 --> 00:20:15,759
to help the abject.

341
00:20:15,839 --> 00:20:17,599
I bought these from her.

342
00:20:22,099 --> 00:20:23,299
Do come again.

343
00:20:52,700 --> 00:20:53,339
Hello.

344
00:20:58,839 --> 00:20:59,539
Ma'am...

345
00:21:06,700 --> 00:21:07,539
How have you been?

346
00:21:26,119 --> 00:21:26,859
Ma'am.

347
00:21:35,799 --> 00:21:37,119
There was an accident.

348
00:21:38,480 --> 00:21:39,759
The baby...

349
00:21:43,039 --> 00:21:44,039
I lost the baby.

350
00:21:51,920 --> 00:21:52,599
Perhaps

351
00:21:52,599 --> 00:21:54,220
we are the definition of tragedy after all.

352
00:21:56,119 --> 00:21:57,660
This should be the end

353
00:21:58,859 --> 00:22:00,319
of me and him, too.

354
00:22:01,980 --> 00:22:02,799
Ma'am.

355
00:22:03,539 --> 00:22:05,319
There must be some misunderstanding.

356
00:22:06,039 --> 00:22:07,039
Changxuan would never

357
00:22:07,039 --> 00:22:08,000
have hurt your mother.

358
00:22:08,279 --> 00:22:09,339
Surely you know

359
00:22:09,339 --> 00:22:10,380
how much he loves you.

360
00:22:10,799 --> 00:22:11,420
How could he...

361
00:22:11,420 --> 00:22:12,700
He wouldn't even start to think

362
00:22:12,839 --> 00:22:14,539
about hurting the person dearest to you?

363
00:22:14,640 --> 00:22:15,519
He just wouldn't.

364
00:22:19,339 --> 00:22:20,799
His love for me...

365
00:22:21,539 --> 00:22:22,980
I've never doubted it.

366
00:22:24,119 --> 00:22:25,480
But now,

367
00:22:26,299 --> 00:22:27,779
everything that happened

368
00:22:27,779 --> 00:22:29,160
has come back to me.

369
00:22:29,920 --> 00:22:32,039
Lately, I keep thinking...

370
00:22:33,920 --> 00:22:35,279
If he and I

371
00:22:35,279 --> 00:22:36,920
had never become entangled,

372
00:22:37,420 --> 00:22:38,880
my mother would still be alive.

373
00:22:40,380 --> 00:22:43,140
Now my mother's gone,

374
00:22:44,119 --> 00:22:45,519
and so is my baby.

375
00:22:47,539 --> 00:22:48,660
All of this

376
00:22:50,660 --> 00:22:51,779
has to end, too.

377
00:22:52,079 --> 00:22:53,819
But he's so worried about you.

378
00:22:54,180 --> 00:22:54,940
He's been

379
00:22:54,940 --> 00:22:55,900
up all night,

380
00:22:55,900 --> 00:22:56,779
unable to sleep.

381
00:22:57,220 --> 00:22:57,740
He's afraid

382
00:22:57,740 --> 00:22:58,660
that alone and pregnant,

383
00:22:58,660 --> 00:22:59,720
you'll struggle

384
00:22:59,759 --> 00:23:00,880
and neglect yourself.

385
00:23:02,220 --> 00:23:02,940
Ma'am.

386
00:23:04,279 --> 00:23:05,240
Come back with me.

387
00:23:13,119 --> 00:23:13,920
Captain Gu.

388
00:23:16,160 --> 00:23:16,900
Could you pretend

389
00:23:16,900 --> 00:23:18,339
you never saw me?

390
00:23:27,460 --> 00:23:28,220
I'm sorry.

391
00:23:31,180 --> 00:23:32,599
I can't lie to Changxuan.

392
00:23:42,319 --> 00:23:43,160
All I want

393
00:23:43,160 --> 00:23:45,539
is to keep living this quiet life.

394
00:23:51,140 --> 00:23:52,700
I'm begging you.

395
00:24:15,200 --> 00:24:16,720
Well? Did you find her?

396
00:24:17,779 --> 00:24:18,460
I checked.

397
00:24:20,640 --> 00:24:21,559
It wasn't her.

398
00:24:59,640 --> 00:25:00,460
Pingjun.

399
00:25:05,440 --> 00:25:07,279
Where are you?

400
00:25:47,119 --> 00:25:47,779
Gentlemen.

401
00:25:48,819 --> 00:25:50,240
The southern revolutionary army

402
00:25:50,799 --> 00:25:51,759
is sweeping all before it.

403
00:25:52,480 --> 00:25:54,079
General Xu has ordered us

404
00:25:54,319 --> 00:25:55,480
to set aside our differences,

405
00:25:56,400 --> 00:25:57,519
form a National Security Army,

406
00:25:58,079 --> 00:25:59,059
and face our common foe.

407
00:26:00,240 --> 00:26:00,539
Now

408
00:26:00,539 --> 00:26:02,700
this alliance demands unity at all ranks.

409
00:26:03,640 --> 00:26:04,299
At present,

410
00:26:05,980 --> 00:26:07,799
the Yu Army's forces

411
00:26:07,940 --> 00:26:08,799
are the strongest

412
00:26:09,079 --> 00:26:10,160
and the best equipped.

413
00:26:11,099 --> 00:26:12,059
In my view,

414
00:26:12,119 --> 00:26:13,259
to show their commitment,

415
00:26:14,099 --> 00:26:16,859
the Yus should lead by example

416
00:26:17,259 --> 00:26:19,299
and place their strongest force,

417
00:26:19,859 --> 00:26:22,680
the 9th Army, under allied command.

418
00:26:23,579 --> 00:26:24,980
That's out of the question.

419
00:26:26,539 --> 00:26:28,319
The Yus would never agree.

420
00:26:31,039 --> 00:26:32,019
Straight away, you

421
00:26:32,019 --> 00:26:33,759
aim for our elite 9th Army.

422
00:26:34,480 --> 00:26:35,680
Quite a demand.

423
00:26:36,400 --> 00:26:37,380
I wonder,

424
00:26:38,059 --> 00:26:39,420
is this the government's wish,

425
00:26:40,500 --> 00:26:41,240
or did Mr. Jiang

426
00:26:41,240 --> 00:26:42,380
take it upon himself to decide?

427
00:26:46,440 --> 00:26:48,319
You evade the question, Deputy Commander.

428
00:26:49,279 --> 00:26:50,039
Is it

429
00:26:50,319 --> 00:26:52,440
that you refuse the government's orders,

430
00:26:52,440 --> 00:26:54,920
or do you have other designs?

431
00:27:03,680 --> 00:27:04,880
We agree

432
00:27:06,200 --> 00:27:09,259
to place the 9th Army in the joint force.

433
00:27:19,240 --> 00:27:20,079
However,

434
00:27:21,220 --> 00:27:22,799
if we're to have a unified command,

435
00:27:23,799 --> 00:27:25,019
a capable commander-in-chief

436
00:27:25,019 --> 00:27:26,119
is to be unanimously elected.

437
00:27:27,359 --> 00:27:28,220
I propose

438
00:27:29,059 --> 00:27:30,079
that the entire joint force

439
00:27:30,079 --> 00:27:31,299
be placed under Yu command.

440
00:27:31,779 --> 00:27:32,559
Agreed?

441
00:27:33,980 --> 00:27:34,880
Out of the question.

442
00:27:36,980 --> 00:27:38,279
How could we agree to that?

443
00:27:42,859 --> 00:27:43,980
Mr. Yu.

444
00:27:46,640 --> 00:27:48,619
The government has always trusted you.

445
00:27:48,859 --> 00:27:51,500
Now, with the nation in peril,

446
00:27:51,839 --> 00:27:54,019
it orders you to join the war effort.

447
00:27:54,180 --> 00:27:55,039
Yet you

448
00:27:56,119 --> 00:27:56,779
seek to overstep

449
00:27:56,779 --> 00:27:58,920
and take command of every force.

450
00:27:59,319 --> 00:28:00,400
Are you trying

451
00:28:01,420 --> 00:28:03,519
to dictate terms to the government?

452
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:09,720
Changxuan.

453
00:28:11,539 --> 00:28:12,920
Commanding the allied forces

454
00:28:12,920 --> 00:28:14,180
is a grave responsibility.

455
00:28:14,900 --> 00:28:16,119
It calls for a respected veteran

456
00:28:16,119 --> 00:28:18,339
with the greatest seniority.

457
00:28:19,579 --> 00:28:21,579
Your ambition is commendable.

458
00:28:22,000 --> 00:28:22,940
Your elders here

459
00:28:22,940 --> 00:28:24,279
will make allowances for you.

460
00:28:27,619 --> 00:28:28,779
You all know

461
00:28:28,920 --> 00:28:30,460
men and officers must know each other

462
00:28:30,839 --> 00:28:32,099
to prevail in battle.

463
00:28:33,720 --> 00:28:35,880
Their tactics and maneuvers

464
00:28:36,480 --> 00:28:37,200
are best

465
00:28:37,200 --> 00:28:38,960
understood by our own officers.

466
00:28:40,220 --> 00:28:41,740
If I hand them over

467
00:28:41,799 --> 00:28:43,119
to unfamiliar commanders,

468
00:28:43,940 --> 00:28:45,259
poor coordination

469
00:28:45,740 --> 00:28:46,980
on the battlefield

470
00:28:47,380 --> 00:28:48,619
could needlessly cost

471
00:28:48,619 --> 00:28:49,420
my men their lives.

472
00:28:50,299 --> 00:28:51,539
I cannot allow that.

473
00:28:52,000 --> 00:28:53,220
He has a point.

474
00:28:53,400 --> 00:28:54,339
Last minute change

475
00:28:54,339 --> 00:28:56,299
of commanders is a cardinal military error.

476
00:28:56,619 --> 00:28:57,420
Exactly.

477
00:28:57,819 --> 00:28:59,440
In his position,

478
00:28:59,799 --> 00:29:00,799
I'd refuse, too.

479
00:29:01,140 --> 00:29:02,680
If neither knows the other,

480
00:29:02,839 --> 00:29:03,339
how can they

481
00:29:03,519 --> 00:29:04,640
fight a war?

482
00:29:07,079 --> 00:29:08,059
Our terms

483
00:29:08,420 --> 00:29:09,500
have been made clear.

484
00:29:09,980 --> 00:29:10,759
Good day.

485
00:29:19,259 --> 00:29:20,079
This meeting

486
00:29:21,200 --> 00:29:22,319
is not over.

487
00:29:23,839 --> 00:29:26,279
If you walk out now, Deputy Commander,

488
00:29:27,099 --> 00:29:28,779
chances are that you'll

489
00:29:28,819 --> 00:29:30,099
get yourself ill-judged

490
00:29:30,759 --> 00:29:32,299
as a coward, saving only his own skin.

491
00:29:36,039 --> 00:29:37,759
I've been ordered to arrange the troops

492
00:29:38,839 --> 00:29:40,539
precisely to prevent the government

493
00:29:41,000 --> 00:29:42,420
from forming

494
00:29:43,140 --> 00:29:45,259
any mistaken impressions of you.

495
00:29:46,099 --> 00:29:47,480
If you leave now,

496
00:29:48,079 --> 00:29:49,160
the consequences

497
00:29:50,079 --> 00:29:51,400
will fall on more shoulders

498
00:29:51,400 --> 00:29:52,980
than yours alone.

499
00:29:59,420 --> 00:30:02,599
Twisting the truth with a stroke of a pen

500
00:30:03,440 --> 00:30:04,859
is your specialty, Mr. Jiang.

501
00:30:05,640 --> 00:30:07,079
No one can rival you on that.

502
00:30:07,420 --> 00:30:08,240
Still,

503
00:30:09,400 --> 00:30:10,640
those of us who've braved gunfire

504
00:30:10,640 --> 00:30:12,460
and fought our way through hell

505
00:30:13,480 --> 00:30:15,039
see things differently.

506
00:30:15,839 --> 00:30:16,720
We won't gamble

507
00:30:16,720 --> 00:30:18,640
with our men's lives.

508
00:30:19,640 --> 00:30:22,480
If anyone tries to use this against us,

509
00:30:24,119 --> 00:30:26,000
the authorities can judge for themselves.

510
00:30:31,180 --> 00:30:31,740
This meeting

511
00:30:32,460 --> 00:30:33,799
may continue without me.

512
00:30:34,480 --> 00:30:35,480
Whatever you decide,

513
00:30:35,619 --> 00:30:36,900
just send someone to inform me.

514
00:30:37,839 --> 00:30:39,380
Got much to attend to with my army.

515
00:30:40,059 --> 00:30:41,480
I can't linger here.

516
00:30:55,859 --> 00:30:57,039
Freshly steamed! Come take a look!

517
00:31:00,140 --> 00:31:01,220
Piping hot buns! Fresh buns!

518
00:31:54,660 --> 00:31:55,279
Miss Ye.

519
00:31:55,460 --> 00:31:56,480
The flowers for Mr. Zhang

520
00:31:56,480 --> 00:31:57,200
are here.

521
00:31:57,839 --> 00:31:58,920
All right. Leave them there.

522
00:31:58,920 --> 00:31:59,599
I'll deliver them later.

523
00:31:59,940 --> 00:32:00,299
Right.

524
00:32:27,700 --> 00:32:29,019
Come look at the flowers!

525
00:32:30,240 --> 00:32:31,319
Look at this. Lovely, isn't it?

526
00:32:31,319 --> 00:32:32,539
Meat buns!

527
00:32:34,759 --> 00:32:35,259
Take your pick.

528
00:32:35,259 --> 00:32:36,079
Anything you like!

529
00:32:38,759 --> 00:32:39,240
All right.

530
00:32:39,940 --> 00:32:40,740
I'll wrap it up.

531
00:32:41,400 --> 00:32:43,099
Mr. Liang? Hanzhi?

532
00:32:43,839 --> 00:32:45,299
What are you two doing together?

533
00:32:45,319 --> 00:32:46,259
Don't let them escape!

534
00:32:46,559 --> 00:32:47,059
Quick!

535
00:32:48,180 --> 00:32:48,579
What are you...

536
00:32:54,299 --> 00:32:55,319
Don't let them escape!

537
00:32:56,900 --> 00:32:58,180
After them! Just ahead!

538
00:33:03,299 --> 00:33:04,099
My flowers!

539
00:33:04,940 --> 00:33:06,140
Watch where you're going!

540
00:33:06,799 --> 00:33:07,339
Tell me.

541
00:33:07,700 --> 00:33:08,720
Did you just see

542
00:33:08,720 --> 00:33:10,259
three people run past here?

543
00:33:10,759 --> 00:33:11,500
A man and a woman

544
00:33:11,500 --> 00:33:12,880
helping an injured woman.

545
00:33:13,960 --> 00:33:15,079
If you saw them, speak up.

546
00:33:15,180 --> 00:33:16,160
They're Communists.

547
00:33:18,940 --> 00:33:19,839
Three people?

548
00:33:20,440 --> 00:33:21,240
Oh, I remember.

549
00:33:21,400 --> 00:33:22,339
Yes, there were three.

550
00:33:22,559 --> 00:33:23,920
They were running quite fast.

551
00:33:24,200 --> 00:33:24,980
Which way?

552
00:33:25,259 --> 00:33:26,480
I think...

553
00:33:26,819 --> 00:33:27,920
they went that way.

554
00:33:28,079 --> 00:33:28,940
Toward the alley.

555
00:33:29,460 --> 00:33:29,900
After them!

556
00:33:32,799 --> 00:33:33,180
Move!

557
00:33:45,819 --> 00:33:47,099
After leaving Nanhuai,

558
00:33:47,519 --> 00:33:49,319
I went to medical school in Guangzhou.

559
00:33:49,900 --> 00:33:51,000
All I wanted

560
00:33:51,119 --> 00:33:52,519
was to heal people and save lives.

561
00:33:53,400 --> 00:33:54,579
At a hometown association gathering,

562
00:33:54,900 --> 00:33:56,380
I met Wenbo and the others.

563
00:33:57,220 --> 00:33:57,859
By then,

564
00:33:58,319 --> 00:33:59,680
he'd moved from staging modern plays

565
00:33:59,799 --> 00:34:01,059
to making patriotic films.

566
00:34:02,019 --> 00:34:02,960
At first,

567
00:34:03,460 --> 00:34:04,839
I wanted to heal people's bodies,

568
00:34:05,279 --> 00:34:06,579
and he wanted to heal their minds.

569
00:34:08,380 --> 00:34:09,739
But then we realized

570
00:34:11,239 --> 00:34:12,639
the nation itself was gravely ill.

571
00:34:13,400 --> 00:34:15,099
You could cure someone's illness,

572
00:34:15,719 --> 00:34:17,420
and still find this person starved to death.

573
00:34:18,019 --> 00:34:19,460
You could awaken someone's mind,

574
00:34:19,980 --> 00:34:21,280
and find this person perish under

575
00:34:21,340 --> 00:34:22,739
the colonizers' and warlords' bullets.

576
00:34:23,320 --> 00:34:24,300
It never addressed the cause.

577
00:34:25,039 --> 00:34:25,559
It couldn't end

578
00:34:25,559 --> 00:34:27,239
the chaos that kept people in misery.

579
00:34:28,659 --> 00:34:29,400
Pingjun.

580
00:34:30,179 --> 00:34:31,119
Our organization

581
00:34:31,519 --> 00:34:32,800
wants more people

582
00:34:33,159 --> 00:34:34,559
to truly open their eyes,

583
00:34:35,340 --> 00:34:36,260
to stop being numb,

584
00:34:36,920 --> 00:34:38,079
to stop being at others' mercy,

585
00:34:38,980 --> 00:34:40,380
and together help our country,

586
00:34:41,219 --> 00:34:42,539
the whole Chinese nation,

587
00:34:42,980 --> 00:34:43,460
find

588
00:34:43,460 --> 00:34:44,760
a path to a true rebirth.

589
00:34:48,780 --> 00:34:50,320
I'm sorry, Pingjun.

590
00:34:51,380 --> 00:34:52,820
We've kept this from you

591
00:34:53,340 --> 00:34:55,039
because, in the current climate,

592
00:34:55,480 --> 00:34:57,059
our work is so dangerous.

593
00:34:57,840 --> 00:34:59,079
Given your connections,

594
00:34:59,639 --> 00:35:00,440
we couldn't risk

595
00:35:00,440 --> 00:35:01,679
drawing you into this.

596
00:35:02,340 --> 00:35:03,139
Hanzhi.

597
00:35:03,820 --> 00:35:04,519
Why would you

598
00:35:04,519 --> 00:35:05,639
need to apologize to me?

599
00:35:06,579 --> 00:35:08,099
In times like these,

600
00:35:08,380 --> 00:35:09,760
awakening the people

601
00:35:09,900 --> 00:35:11,320
and saving lives

602
00:35:11,900 --> 00:35:13,239
is easy enough to talk about,

603
00:35:13,599 --> 00:35:15,079
but so hard to do.

604
00:35:15,639 --> 00:35:18,039
Yet you're willing to stand up and act.

605
00:35:18,280 --> 00:35:19,480
That kind of courage

606
00:35:19,579 --> 00:35:21,059
is something I deeply admire.

607
00:35:21,639 --> 00:35:22,340
I know

608
00:35:22,679 --> 00:35:23,679
there's only so much

609
00:35:23,679 --> 00:35:24,880
I can do on my own.

610
00:35:25,579 --> 00:35:26,820
But in the future,

611
00:35:27,219 --> 00:35:28,059
if there's anything

612
00:35:28,059 --> 00:35:29,639
I can help you with,

613
00:35:30,039 --> 00:35:32,460
please, please let me be part of it.

614
00:35:50,940 --> 00:35:51,860
How's it going?

615
00:35:52,119 --> 00:35:53,800
Everything's being done as you asked.

616
00:35:54,119 --> 00:35:54,900
Each day, I arrange for

617
00:35:54,900 --> 00:35:55,860
someone different to order flowers.

618
00:35:55,900 --> 00:35:57,039
She won't suspect a thing.

619
00:35:57,119 --> 00:35:58,820
Good. Well done.

620
00:36:01,679 --> 00:36:02,480
Thank you.

621
00:36:19,639 --> 00:36:20,380
Deputy Commander, sir.

622
00:36:37,400 --> 00:36:37,820
Changxuan.

623
00:36:38,559 --> 00:36:39,280
In today's drill,

624
00:36:39,460 --> 00:36:40,219
the 9th Army's 3rd Regiment

625
00:36:40,219 --> 00:36:41,340
split into opposing teams.

626
00:36:41,719 --> 00:36:43,139
The focus was on bayonet combat,

627
00:36:43,239 --> 00:36:44,000
charging techniques,

628
00:36:44,239 --> 00:36:45,519
and maintaining assault formations.

629
00:36:51,840 --> 00:36:53,539
I hear that in Siping,

630
00:36:55,480 --> 00:36:57,440
you have a special lady friend.

631
00:37:00,659 --> 00:37:01,320
What?

632
00:37:02,960 --> 00:37:04,619
You're keeping secrets even from me?

633
00:37:08,539 --> 00:37:10,340
The woman who runs that flower shop...

634
00:37:12,840 --> 00:37:13,639
Who is she?

635
00:37:23,699 --> 00:37:24,320
It's Pingjun.

636
00:37:27,659 --> 00:37:29,139
She's the one running the shop.

637
00:37:30,780 --> 00:37:31,699
Why didn't you tell me?

638
00:37:31,760 --> 00:37:32,900
Why didn't you tell me?

639
00:37:33,119 --> 00:37:34,400
I asked you so many times!

640
00:37:38,199 --> 00:37:39,239
How is she?

641
00:37:44,000 --> 00:37:44,639
The baby...

642
00:37:49,019 --> 00:37:49,880
She lost the baby.

643
00:37:57,059 --> 00:37:58,059
The baby's gone?

644
00:38:17,880 --> 00:38:18,519
Ruitong.

645
00:38:20,719 --> 00:38:22,440
We grew up together.

646
00:38:24,260 --> 00:38:27,840
Through all the carnage of battle,

647
00:38:27,880 --> 00:38:29,599
I trusted you to watch my back.

648
00:38:35,179 --> 00:38:37,059
I trusted you more than anyone.

649
00:38:41,960 --> 00:38:43,840
You knew I was searching for Pingjun!

650
00:38:44,039 --> 00:38:45,380
She's my wife!

651
00:38:45,380 --> 00:38:46,519
That was my child!

652
00:38:46,579 --> 00:38:48,039
Why did you keep this from me?

653
00:38:48,039 --> 00:38:49,179
How could you...

654
00:38:49,260 --> 00:38:50,760
How dare you!

655
00:39:15,440 --> 00:39:17,219
I've betrayed your trust.

656
00:39:18,139 --> 00:39:19,139
I withheld the truth.

657
00:39:19,320 --> 00:39:20,420
It's unforgivable.

658
00:39:22,800 --> 00:39:24,559
Punish me under military law.

659
00:39:26,300 --> 00:39:28,559
I'll accept whatever punishment you give.

660
00:40:30,579 --> 00:40:31,079
You really think

661
00:40:31,079 --> 00:40:32,019
I was in the dark?

662
00:40:38,679 --> 00:40:39,199
If I'd known

663
00:40:39,199 --> 00:40:40,980
you'd end up like this,

664
00:40:42,119 --> 00:40:44,119
perhaps I'd have found the courage

665
00:40:45,539 --> 00:40:46,639
to ask Changxuan to let you go.

666
00:41:10,880 --> 00:41:12,179
This is all my fault.

667
00:41:13,760 --> 00:41:14,760
But I've never dared

668
00:41:14,760 --> 00:41:16,119
hope for anything improper.

669
00:41:16,880 --> 00:41:18,619
Nor have I ever meant to betray you.

670
00:41:27,340 --> 00:41:28,420
She wouldn't come back with you,

671
00:41:28,420 --> 00:41:28,900
would she?

672
00:41:35,920 --> 00:41:36,679
She said

673
00:41:38,739 --> 00:41:40,699
she wants to leave the past behind.

674
00:41:41,840 --> 00:41:42,840
She doesn't want anyone

675
00:41:42,840 --> 00:41:43,719
disturbing her again.

676
00:41:49,539 --> 00:41:50,420
Some things,

677
00:41:52,400 --> 00:41:53,719
when you know they can never be,

678
00:41:55,059 --> 00:41:56,559
you must give up for good.

679
00:41:58,559 --> 00:41:59,699
Your loyalty,

680
00:42:00,360 --> 00:42:01,599
your duty...

681
00:42:03,159 --> 00:42:05,480
Neither allows you to step out of line.

682
00:42:08,139 --> 00:42:08,940
Otherwise,

683
00:42:12,019 --> 00:42:13,860
you're only tormenting yourself.

684
00:44:07,679 --> 00:44:09,219
I know what you're going to say.

685
00:44:11,199 --> 00:44:12,420
But, Yu Changxuan,

686
00:44:16,340 --> 00:44:17,840
I'm not going back with you.

687
00:44:19,820 --> 00:44:21,500
I won't confess to something I didn't do.

688
00:44:24,820 --> 00:44:25,760
I just want us

689
00:44:27,360 --> 00:44:30,000
to clear things up between us.

690
00:44:32,260 --> 00:44:33,699
Have you ever thought

691
00:44:35,519 --> 00:44:36,900
that perhaps,

692
00:44:38,679 --> 00:44:40,179
this relationship of ours

693
00:44:41,460 --> 00:44:43,059
was never built to last?

694
00:44:54,320 --> 00:44:55,480
I've never believed in fate.

695
00:44:57,900 --> 00:44:59,099
And I won't bow to it.

696
00:45:01,840 --> 00:45:03,179
Neither would I have.

697
00:45:04,679 --> 00:45:06,280
But after everything that's happened,

698
00:45:07,699 --> 00:45:08,900
how can I not?

699
00:45:10,760 --> 00:45:12,059
Between us,

700
00:45:12,340 --> 00:45:13,480
there's always been

701
00:45:13,480 --> 00:45:14,579
so much weighing us down.

702
00:45:16,079 --> 00:45:17,440
Every time we draw close,

703
00:45:18,460 --> 00:45:20,099
fate tears us apart.

704
00:45:20,780 --> 00:45:21,860
It's as though we're

705
00:45:21,860 --> 00:45:23,480
from two different worlds,

706
00:45:25,219 --> 00:45:27,039
trying to force a life together.

707
00:45:40,639 --> 00:45:41,639
So you won't give me

708
00:45:41,639 --> 00:45:42,820
even one more chance?

709
00:45:48,260 --> 00:45:49,360
Lately,

710
00:45:50,340 --> 00:45:51,719
I've often found myself thinking.

711
00:45:53,980 --> 00:45:55,639
So much of our lives

712
00:45:56,460 --> 00:45:57,500
is spent

713
00:45:57,960 --> 00:45:59,820
caught in the bonds of love.

714
00:46:01,280 --> 00:46:03,159
All that love and resentment

715
00:46:04,099 --> 00:46:05,199
can wear one out,

716
00:46:05,199 --> 00:46:06,579
with no more joy or sorrow left to feel.

717
00:46:08,099 --> 00:46:10,699
Now that I've stepped beyond it,

718
00:46:12,079 --> 00:46:13,460
I've suddenly realized something.

719
00:46:16,260 --> 00:46:17,840
In times like these,

720
00:46:18,760 --> 00:46:20,280
with our country in turmoil,

721
00:46:21,679 --> 00:46:23,139
however much it hurts,

722
00:46:23,900 --> 00:46:24,619
it's but one

723
00:46:24,619 --> 00:46:26,280
insignificant fraction of the wider struggle.

724
00:46:27,599 --> 00:46:29,239
I no longer want to dwell on

725
00:46:29,320 --> 00:46:30,960
whether someone loves me,

726
00:46:32,199 --> 00:46:33,760
or see myself trapped in

727
00:46:34,039 --> 00:46:35,679
the resentment against someone.

728
00:46:41,860 --> 00:46:43,219
Rather than live as your wife,

729
00:46:44,400 --> 00:46:45,840
I want to go out into the world

730
00:46:47,579 --> 00:46:49,320
and do something more meaningful.

731
00:46:52,400 --> 00:46:53,960
In this world,

732
00:46:54,559 --> 00:46:55,960
there's more than one path to take.

733
00:46:57,440 --> 00:46:59,059
You have your responsibilities.

734
00:46:59,599 --> 00:47:01,199
I have my own path to follow.

735
00:47:01,460 --> 00:47:02,579
So now,

736
00:47:08,400 --> 00:47:09,179
I hope you can

737
00:47:09,179 --> 00:47:10,360
respect my choice.

738
00:47:17,460 --> 00:47:18,079
All right.

739
00:47:19,760 --> 00:47:20,780
I promised you

740
00:47:21,760 --> 00:47:23,360
I'd never force you into anything again.

741
00:47:29,719 --> 00:47:31,139
I'll respect your choice.

742
00:47:44,820 --> 00:47:45,800
About your mother...

743
00:47:48,239 --> 00:47:49,239
I know all the evidence

744
00:47:49,239 --> 00:47:50,260
points to me.

745
00:47:52,820 --> 00:47:53,840
I won't argue my innocence.

746
00:47:55,760 --> 00:47:57,380
But please give me a little more time.

747
00:47:59,820 --> 00:48:01,000
I promise you

748
00:48:02,719 --> 00:48:03,460
and her

749
00:48:05,380 --> 00:48:06,380
the answers you deserve.
